.TH COUNT_FILES 1 "14 Oct 2026" "count-files 2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
count_files \- count files, directories and links in the specified directory or, if the parameter is not passed, in /etc
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B count_files
[\fIDIRECTORY\fR] [\fIEXTENSION\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B A Bash script that counts the number of files, directories and symbolic links in the specified directory or, if the parameter is not passed, in the /etc directory. By default, it filters files by the .conf extension and also shows the total size and generation timestamp.
